  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the Socio-economic Integration of Vulnerable Host Community Members and Mobile Populations in Libya Through Youth Employment One Stop Shops (YESS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Libya is a primary transit and destination country for thousands of migrants, mainly from the neighbouring countries seeking employment opportunities. Many of them face tremendous socio-economic integration challenges, including discrimination and human rights violations in Libya. To help improve labour conditions and increasing employment and livelihood opportunities in an inclusive manner for both migrants and host-community in Libya, IOM in collaboration with the Ministry of Labour and Rehabilitation has established two Youth Employment One Stop Shop (YESS) and is setting up groundwork towards the establishment of a third one in south Libya.In an effort to strengthen the employability of vulnerable host community members and mobile populations in Libya, IOM assesses labour market demands, and projected labour force needs, and closely cooperates with the Ministry of Labour and Rehabilitation on technical support, institutional capacity building, and tailormade training curricula aimed at equipping target beneficiaries with highly-sought-after technical skills. The overall objective of this project is to promote socio-economic integration and social cohesion of vulnerable groups, including mobile populations and host communities. IOM will continue and scale up YESS centres activities to promote integration and an inclusive labour force to develop Libyan local economies.</narrative>
  </description>
